2026-10-28T16:56:21.5027905Z {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgUzE1TjZti4sZygkEP5j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Bv6ea5f1aaHj3dxaLu8Fqq","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/gh-aw/agent/issue.json"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6008,"cache_read_input_tokens":24861,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6008,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ac8c3e1c-998e-40c1-bfb4-2830836ba3ca","uuid":"e7c3edba-c49a-4bd3-9059-d2667151a1f0","timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:56:21.499Z","request_id":"req_011CgUzE16A26LLzNuu8xWi7"}
2026-10-28T16:56:21.5234449Z {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bv6ea5f1aaHj3dxaLu8Fqq","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"number\": 5,\n3\t  \"url\": \"https://github.com/wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent/issues/5\",\n4\t  \"repo\": \"wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent\",\n5\t  \"title\": \"aws_cognito_user_pool: invite_message_template without sms_message sends an empty SMSMessage and UpdateUserPool fails\",\n6\t  \"body\": \"### Terraform and AWS Provider Version\\n\\nTerraform 1.15.9, hashicorp/aws 6.66.0\\n\\n### Affected Resource(s) or Data Source(s)\\n\\n- `aws_cognito_user_pool`\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nSetting `admin_create_user_config.invite_message_template` with `email_subject` and `email_message` only, leaving the optional `sms_message` unset, should update the pool. The field is documented as optional, and the pool has no SMS configuration, so no SMS message is ever sent.\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\n`terraform plan` succeeds and shows the expected in-place update. `terraform apply` fails: the provider sends `SMSMessage: \\\"\\\"` in the `UpdateUserPool` request, and Cognito rejects it because an SMS message must be between 6 and 140 characters. The whole pool update is refused, including unrelated changes in the same apply.\\n\\nCause: `expandAdminCreateUserConfigType` in `internal/service/cognitoidp/user_pool.go` sets `EmailMessage`, `EmailSubject` and `SMSMessage` whenever the key is present in the block's map, which for a schema attribute is always, so an unset `sms_message` becomes an empty string. `expandVerificationMessageTemplateType` in the same file guards each field with `v.(string) != \\\"\\\"` and does not have this problem.\\n\\n### Relevant Error/Panic Output\\n\\n```\\nError: updating Cognito User Pool (eu-west-2_XXXXXXXXX): operation error Cognito Identity Provider: UpdateUserPool, https response error StatusCode: 400, RequestID: c334be80-5195-4df1-bf38-794958da5181, InvalidParameterException: 1 validation error detected: Value '' at 'adminCreateUserConfig.inviteMessageTemplate.sMSMessage' failed to satisfy constraint: Member must have length greater than or equal to 6\\n```\\n\\n### Sample Terraform Configuration\\n\\n```hcl\\nresource \\\"aws_cognito_user_pool\\\" \\\"example\\\" {\\n  name = \\\"example\\\"\\n\\n  username_attributes      = [\\\"email\\\"]\\n  auto_verified_attributes = [\\\"email\\\"]\\n\\n  admin_create_user_config {\\n    invite_message_template {\\n      email_subject = \\\"Your account\\\"\\n      email_message = \\\"<p>Sign in with this temporary password: {####}</p><p>Sent to {username}.</p>\\\"\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Steps to Reproduce\\n\\n1. Apply the pool without the `admin_create_user_config` block.\\n2. Add the block above, with `email_subject` and `email_message` but no `sms_message`.\\n3. `terraform plan` shows one in-place update.\\n4. `terraform apply` fails with the error above.\\n\\nWorkaround: set `sms_message` to any valid value containing `{username}` and `{####}`, for example `\\\"Temporary password for {username}: {####}\\\"`, even though it is never sent.\\n\\n### Debug Logging\\n\\nNot captured; the apply ran in CI. The error message shows the empty value the provider sent.\\n\\n### GenAI / LLM Assisted Development\\n\\nThis report was drafted with an AI assistant (Claude Code). The error output, the reproduction and the reading of the provider source were checked by a person against a real apply.\\n\\n### Important Factoids\\n\\nThe pool uses `username_attributes = [\\\"email\\\"]` and has no `sms_configuration`. The same template fields in `verification_message_template` are handled with empty-string guards, so the inconsistency is specific to `invite_message_template`.\\n\\n### References\\n\\n- `#13060` reported the same error in 2020 and was closed as stale in 2024.\\n- AWS API reference for `MessageTemplateType`: `SMSMessage` is optional, 6 to 140 characters.\\n\\n### Would you like to implement a fix?\\n\\nMaybe. The fix looks like the `!= \\\"\\\"` guards already used in `expandVerificationMessageTemplateType`.\\n\\n\",\n7\t  \"author\": \"zzzinn\",\n8\t  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n9\t  \"labels\": [],\n10\t  \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T16:53:50Z\",\n11\t  \"as_of\": \"2026-10-20T12:30:21Z\"\n12\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ac8c3e1c-998e-40c1-bfb4-2830836ba3ca","uuid":"aa3dbe2d-68a4-4db3-9707-30e246b79c2a","timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:56:21.517Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/gh-aw/agent/issue.json","content":"{\n  \"number\": 5,\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent/issues/5\",\n  \"repo\": \"wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent\",\n  \"title\": \"aws_cognito_user_pool: invite_message_template without sms_message sends an empty SMSMessage and UpdateUserPool fails\",\n  \"body\": \"### Terraform and AWS Provider Version\\n\\nTerraform 1.15.9, hashicorp/aws 6.66.0\\n\\n### Affected Resource(s) or Data Source(s)\\n\\n- `aws_cognito_user_pool`\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nSetting `admin_create_user_config.invite_message_template` with `email_subject` and `email_message` only, leaving the optional `sms_message` unset, should update the pool. The field is documented as optional, and the pool has no SMS configuration, so no SMS message is ever sent.\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\n`terraform plan` succeeds and shows the expected in-place update. `terraform apply` fails: the provider sends `SMSMessage: \\\"\\\"` in the `UpdateUserPool` request, and Cognito rejects it because an SMS message must be between 6 and 140 characters. The whole pool update is refused, including unrelated changes in the same apply.\\n\\nCause: `expandAdminCreateUserConfigType` in `internal/service/cognitoidp/user_pool.go` sets `EmailMessage`, `EmailSubject` and `SMSMessage` whenever the key is present in the block's map, which for a schema attribute is always, so an unset `sms_message` becomes an empty string. `expandVerificationMessageTemplateType` in the same file guards each field with `v.(string) != \\\"\\\"` and does not have this problem.\\n\\n### Relevant Error/Panic Output\\n\\n```\\nError: updating Cognito User Pool (eu-west-2_XXXXXXXXX): operation error Cognito Identity Provider: UpdateUserPool, https response error StatusCode: 400, RequestID: c334be80-5195-4df1-bf38-794958da5181, InvalidParameterException: 1 validation error detected: Value '' at 'adminCreateUserConfig.inviteMessageTemplate.sMSMessage' failed to satisfy constraint: Member must have length greater than or equal to 6\\n```\\n\\n### Sample Terraform Configuration\\n\\n```hcl\\nresource \\\"aws_cognito_user_pool\\\" \\\"example\\\" {\\n  name = \\\"example\\\"\\n\\n  username_attributes      = [\\\"email\\\"]\\n  auto_verified_attributes = [\\\"email\\\"]\\n\\n  admin_create_user_config {\\n    invite_message_template {\\n      email_subject = \\\"Your account\\\"\\n      email_message = \\\"<p>Sign in with this temporary password: {####}</p><p>Sent to {username}.</p>\\\"\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Steps to Reproduce\\n\\n1. Apply the pool without the `admin_create_user_config` block.\\n2. Add the block above, with `email_subject` and `email_message` but no `sms_message`.\\n3. `terraform plan` shows one in-place update.\\n4. `terraform apply` fails with the error above.\\n\\nWorkaround: set `sms_message` to any valid value containing `{username}` and `{####}`, for example `\\\"Temporary password for {username}: {####}\\\"`, even though it is never sent.\\n\\n### Debug Logging\\n\\nNot captured; the apply ran in CI. The error message shows the empty value the provider sent.\\n\\n### GenAI / LLM Assisted Development\\n\\nThis report was drafted with an AI assistant (Claude Code). The error output, the reproduction and the reading of the provider source were checked by a person against a real apply.\\n\\n### Important Factoids\\n\\nThe pool uses `username_attributes = [\\\"email\\\"]` and has no `sms_configuration`. The same template fields in `verification_message_template` are handled with empty-string guards, so the inconsistency is specific to `invite_message_template`.\\n\\n### References\\n\\n- `#13060` reported the same error in 2020 and was closed as stale in 2024.\\n- AWS API reference for `MessageTemplateType`: `SMSMessage` is optional, 6 to 140 characters.\\n\\n### Would you like to implement a fix?\\n\\nMaybe. The fix looks like the `!= \\\"\\\"` guards already used in `expandVerificationMessageTemplateType`.\\n\\n\",\n  \"author\": \"zzzinn\",\n  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n  \"labels\": [],\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T16:53:50Z\",\n  \"as_of\": \"2026-10-20T12:30:21Z\"\n}","numLines":12,"startLine":1,"totalLines":12}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Bv6ea5f1aaHj3dxaLu8Fqq","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
